<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">South China Sea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> Sea is a marginal sea of the Pacific bordered by southern China, mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>. It carried maritime trade between China and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a> profile notes that Srivijaya controlled shipping between the Indian Ocean and the South China Sea, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> profile discusses maritime commerce through it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-china-sea.jpg" alt="South China Sea" width="320" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Serg!o · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mar_de_China_Meridional_-_BM_WMS_2004.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
